      "verification_status": "verified_primary",
      "last_verified": "2026-08-10",
      "notes": "VERIFIED against the enrolled text 2026-08-10. Enacts Utah Code ch. 63G-31. Eleven enumerated categories; 'human being' is defined as 'a member of the species classified as Homo sapiens', which is the taxonomic anchor. 'Legal personhood' is defined to cover BOTH the rights/obligations of an individual AND of 'a person other than an individual', i.e. it reaches juridical personhood - relevant to the zero-member LLC question. 'Governmental entity' includes a court, the Legislature, and bodies with adjudicatory or rulemaking authority. Bars only granting NEW personhood, so needs no corporate saving clause. Triggered Ban v. Utah (NhRP), dismissed May 2025. Senate sponsor Don L. Ipson is not named in the paper.",
